{"name":"Tree Poppy","hex":"#e2813b","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tree poppy","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Synonym of Matilija poppy (Romneya)","Any member of the genus Dendromecon, including:\nbush poppy (Dendromecon rigida)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tree_poppy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tree poppy","blocks":[{"text":"Tree poppy is a name used for various plants in the family Papaveraceae:"},{"items":["Genus Dendromecon","Genus Romneya","Bocconia frutescens"]}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tree_poppy","wikidata":"Q15945500"},{"title":"Tree","blocks":[{"text":"In botany, a tree is a perennial plant with an elongated stem, or trunk, usually supporting branches and leaves. In some usages, the definition of a tree may be narrower, e.g., including only woody plants with secondary growth, only plants that are usable for timber, or only plants above a specified height. Wider definitions include taller palms, tree ferns, bananas, and bamboos."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Usamljeni_jasen_-_panoramio_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Usamljeni_jasen_-_panoramio_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tree","wikidata":"Q10884"},{"title":"Poppy","blocks":[{"text":"A poppy is a flowering plant in the subfamily Papaveroideae of the family Papaveraceae. Poppies are herbaceous plants, often grown for their colourful flowers. One species of poppy, Papaver somniferum, is the source of the narcotic drug mixture opium, which contains powerful medicinal alkaloids such as morphine and has been used since ancient times as an analgesic and narcotic medicinal and recreational drug. It also produces edible seeds. Following the trench warfare in the poppy fields of Flanders, Belgium, during World War I, poppies, specifically the red poppy, have become a symbol of remembrance of soldiers who have died during wartime, especially in the UK, Canada, Australia, Africa and other Commonwealth realms."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Poppies_in_the_Sunset_on_Lake_Geneva.jpg/330px-Poppies_in_the_Sunset_on_Lake_Geneva.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poppy","wikidata":"Q967457"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Larix_decidua_Aletschwald.jpg/500px-Larix_decidua_Aletschwald.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Larix_decidua_Aletschwald.jpg/1280px-Larix_decidua_Aletschwald.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Larix_decidua_Aletschwald.jpg/500px-Larix_decidua_Aletschwald.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"European larch (Larix decidua), a coniferous tree which is also deciduous[2]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALarix_decidua_Aletschwald.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Nedravazhakola.jpg/500px-Nedravazhakola.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Nedravazhakola.jpg/1280px-Nedravazhakola.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Nedravazhakola.jpg/500px-Nedravazhakola.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Tall herbaceous monocotyledonous plants such as banana lack secondary growth, so are often not called trees.[9]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANedravazhakola.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/CabbageTreeKaihoka.jpg/500px-CabbageTreeKai